# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — Common Mistakes

The things people get wrong when using this project, and what to do instead.

**One rule governs this entire document: every entry cites a real defect.** Not a hypothetical
misuse, not a style preference, not something a maintainer thinks would be unwise — an actual bug
report, review comment, support question, or broken build that happened. That rule is the template.

Without it this file becomes a list of maintainer opinions dressed as guidance, and it grows without
limit, because there is no shortage of ways to imagine someone being wrong. With it, the file stays
short and every entry has already earned its place by costing somebody time.

Owned by whoever fields the questions.

---

## 1. Adding an entry

Before writing one, answer: **what is the citation?**

<!-- DECIDE: what counts as a citation in this project — an issue number, a PR review link, a
     support thread, a dated incident? Pick the forms you actually have and list them. An entry
     with no citation gets removed, not softened, and that is the rule that keeps this file
     trustworthy. -->

Then check it does not belong somewhere else instead:

| If the mistake is | It belongs in |
|---|---|
| A consumer using the wrong component | That component's page, under "when not to use it" |
| A consumer assembling components wrongly | The patterns document |
| A contributor breaking a project convention | The contributing document |
| A consumer relying on something now changed | The changelog or the deprecation ledger |

**An entry here is the last resort**, for a mistake that has no natural home — or one that keeps
being made *despite* having a home, which is itself a finding about that document.

<!-- DECIDE: if an entry keeps recurring after being documented, what happens? The honest answers
     are: make it impossible in the API, or add a check that catches it. Documentation that has
     failed twice will not succeed on the third reading. Decide which of those this project does,
     so entries can graduate off this list rather than accumulating. -->

